Level 1: GenAI & RAG Basics
GenAI Introduction – Get familiar with what Generative AI is and where it's used.
Basics of LLMs – Understand how Large Language Models are trained and used.
Prompt Engineering – Learn to write effective prompts for better LLM results.
LLM Preprocessing – Clean, chunk, and format data for AI tasks.
RAG Fundamentals – Combine LLMs with search to retrieve accurate information.
Vector Databases – Store and search embeddings using Pinecone, Chroma, etc.
API Wrappers – Interact with LLMs using LangChain, LlamaIndex, or direct APIs.
Tool Integration – Let LLMs call tools like search, code execution, or APIs.



Level 2: AI Agent Essentials
What Are AI Agents? – Learn how agents plan, reason, and act autonomously.
Agentic Frameworks – Explore LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, and similar frameworks.
Build Your First Agent – Create a simple AI agent that performs real tasks.
Agent Workflows – Design how agents think, act, and complete tasks.
Agent Memory – Add memory so agents can recall past actions and context.
Agent Evaluation – Track agent accuracy, performance, and reliability.
Multi-Step Reasoning – Teach agents to think in logical sequences.
Multi-Agent Systems – Enable agents to work together on complex tasks.
Action Planning – Make agents plan, adapt, and retry intelligently.
Safety & Guardrails – Add filters and controls to keep agents safe and factual.



Level 3: Advanced Agent Skills
Real-World Integration – Connect agents to tools like Slack, Notion, Gmail, etc.
Autonomous Loops – Create agents that run and update tasks on their own.
Custom Toolkits – Equip agents with APIs, Python tools, or custom functions.
Optimize Performance – Improve speed, cost efficiency, and error handling.
Deploy to Production – Host and manage AI agents for real users.
